<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
  <title>Team Context Engine | Agentic SE Lab</title>
  <script>
    (() => {
      try {
        const saved = localStorage.getItem("upb-theme");
        const theme = saved === "light" || saved === "dark"
          ? saved
          : (window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "dark" : "light");
        document.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;
      } catch (_) {
        document.documentElement.dataset.theme =
          window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "dark" : "light";
      }
    })();
  </script>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: light;
      --bg: #FFF8E7;
      --text: #1D1D1F;
      --muted: #5A5A5F;
      --card: #FFFFFF;
      --accent: #B7522B;
      --accent-strong: #8E3C20;
      --accent-soft: #F3E2CC;
      --border: #E8DECC;
      --shadow: 0 14px 40px rgba(55, 42, 24, 0.08);
      --header-bg: rgba(255, 248, 231, 0.91);
    }

    html[data-theme="dark"] {
      color-scheme: dark;
      --bg: #14142B;
      --text: #F4F1DE;
      --muted: #B8B5A7;
      --card: #1F1F3D;
      --accent: #F1A47C;
      --accent-strong: #FFC4A4;
      --accent-soft: #34314D;
      --border: #393752;
      --shadow: 0 14px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
      --header-bg: rgba(20, 20, 43, 0.91);
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    html {
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
      scroll-padding-top: 2rem;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.65;
      transition: background-color 180ms ease, color 180ms ease;
    }

    a {
      color: inherit;
    }

    a:focus-visible,
    button:focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--accent);
      outline-offset: 4px;
    }

    .skip-link {
      position: absolute;
      top: 0.75rem;
      left: 1rem;
      z-index: 10;
      padding: 0.7rem 1rem;
      transform: translateY(-160%);
      border-radius: 0.6rem;
      background: var(--card);
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .skip-link:focus {
      transform: translateY(0);
    }

    .site-header {
      position: relative;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .header-inner,
    main,
    .footer-inner {
      width: min(1120px, calc(100% - 3rem));
      margin-inline: auto;
    }

    .header-inner {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 1.1rem 2rem;
      padding-block: 1.5rem;
    }

    .brand {
      display: inline-block;
      width: fit-content;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .brand-name {
      display: block;
      font-size: 1.35rem;
      font-weight: 790;
      letter-spacing: -0.045em;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }

    .tagline {
      margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }

    .header-actions {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: flex-end;
      gap: 1.25rem;
    }

    .site-nav {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 1.35rem;
    }

    .site-nav a {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.92rem;
      font-weight: 620;
      text-decoration: none;
      transition: color 150ms ease;
    }

    .site-nav a:hover {
      color: var(--accent);
    }

    .theme-toggle {
      display: inline-grid;
      width: 2.75rem;
      height: 2.75rem;
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      place-items: center;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--card);
      color: var(--text);
      cursor: pointer;
      font-size: 1.15rem;
      transition: border-color 150ms ease, transform 150ms ease;
    }

    .theme-toggle:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      border-color: var(--accent);
    }

    main {
      padding-block: 2.8rem 5rem;
    }

    .hero {
      position: relative;
      display: grid;
      min-height: 310px;
      align-content: center;
      overflow: hidden;
      padding: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 5.25rem);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 1.5rem;
      background:
        radial-gradient(ellipse at 90% 15%, var(--accent-soft), transparent 48%),
        var(--card);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .hero::after {
      position: absolute;
      right: -3.3rem;
      bottom: -7.5rem;
      width: 19rem;
      height: 19rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 50%;
      content: "";
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
      color: var(--accent-strong);
      font-size: 0.77rem;
      font-weight: 760;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      max-width: 740px;
      margin: 0;
      font-size: clamp(2.7rem, 7.5vw, 5.8rem);
      font-weight: 780;
      letter-spacing: -0.075em;
      line-height: 0.99;
    }

    .hero-copy {
      max-width: 580px;
      margin: 1.2rem 0 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.15rem);
    }

    .hero-label {
      display: inline-flex;
      width: fit-content;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.55rem;
      margin-top: 1.6rem;
      padding: 0.45rem 0.8rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      font-weight: 630;
    }

    .hero-label::before {
      width: 0.48rem;
      height: 0.48rem;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--accent);
      content: "";
    }

    .section {
      padding-top: 5.3rem;
    }

    .section-heading {
      display: flex;
      align-items: end;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 1.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    }

    .section-heading h2 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 3.25rem);
      font-weight: 740;
      letter-spacing: -0.06em;
      line-height: 1.12;
    }

    .section-intro {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 0 0 2rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .team-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1.25rem;
    }

    .member-card {
      min-width: 0;
      overflow: hidden;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 1.15rem;
      background: var(--card);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .member-photo {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      height: 245px;
      object-fit: cover;
      object-position: center 38%;
      background: var(--accent-soft);
    }

    .member-body {
      padding: 1.45rem;
    }

    .member-topline {
      display: flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 0.75rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
    }

    .member-topline h3 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 1.55rem;
      font-weight: 750;
      letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    }

    .semester {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      text-align: right;
    }

    .interests {
      margin: 0.55rem 0 1.15rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.91rem;
    }

    .interests strong {
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .member-card h4 {
      margin: 1.1rem 0 0.3rem;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      font-weight: 740;
      letter-spacing: 0.055em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .member-card p.detail {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.91rem;
    }

    .hot-take {
      margin-top: 1.25rem;
      padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
      border-radius: 0 0.65rem 0.65rem 0;
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 0.91rem;
      font-weight: 610;
    }

    .future-panel {
      padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 1.25rem;
      background: var(--card);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .future-lede {
      max-width: 850px;
      margin: 0 0 2rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }

    .principles {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
      margin-bottom: 2.25rem;
    }

    .principle {
      padding: 1.1rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 0.85rem;
      background: var(--bg);
    }

    .principle-number {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      font-weight: 750;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    }

    .principle h3 {
      margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }

    .principle p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.88rem;
    }

    .forecast-heading {
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    }

    .forecast-list {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 0.85rem;
    }

    .forecast {
      padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 0.85rem;
    }

    .forecast h4 {
      margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
      font-size: 0.92rem;
    }

    .forecast p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.88rem;
    }

    .site-footer {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .footer-inner {
      padding-block: 1.7rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .footer-inner p {
      margin: 0;
    }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .header-inner,
      main,
      .footer-inner {
        width: calc(100% - 2rem);
      }

      .header-inner {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        justify-items: start;
        gap: 1rem;
        padding-block: 1rem;
      }

      .header-actions {
        width: 100%;
        justify-content: space-between;
      }

      .site-nav {
        gap: 1rem;
      }

      main {
        padding-top: 1.25rem;
      }

      .hero {
        min-height: 290px;
        padding: 2rem 1.4rem;
      }

      .team-grid,
      .principles,
      .forecast-list {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .section {
        padding-top: 3.7rem;
      }

      .section-heading {
        align-items: start;
      }

      .member-photo {
        height: 220px;
      }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      *,
      *::before,
      *::after {
        scroll-behavior: auto !important;
        transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#team">Skip to team</a>

  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="header-inner">
      <div>
        <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Context Engine home">
          <span class="brand-name">Context Engine</span>
        </a>
        <p class="tagline">Thoughtful engineering, human by design.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="header-actions">
        <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
          <a href="#team">The team</a>
          <a href="#future-of-se">The future</a>
        </nav>
        <button class="theme-toggle" id="theme-toggle" type="button"
          aria-label="Switch to night mode" aria-pressed="false">
          <span aria-hidden="true">☾</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="top">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Meet the people behind the ideas</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Good engineering starts with good questions.</h1>
      <p class="hero-copy">
        We’re a team of computer scientists exploring how to build software
        that works well, makes sense, and keeps people in the picture.
      </p>
      <span class="hero-label">Agentic Software Engineering · Paderborn University</span>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="team" aria-labelledby="team-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Five perspectives, one team</p>
          <h2 id="team-title">The team</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="section-intro">
        We’re M.Sc. Computer Science students at the Agentic Software Engineering,
        Paderborn University lab. What connects us is curiosity about the systems
        behind software—and the people who depend on it. We bring different
        interests, from distributed infrastructure to human-computer interaction,
        to the same conversation.
      </p>

      <div class="team-grid">
        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:Mohammad.png}}" alt="Mohammad">
          <div class="member-body">
            <div class="member-topline">
              <h3>Mohammad</h3>
              <span class="semester">M.Sc. · 1st semester</span>
            </div>
            <p class="interests"><strong>Into:</strong> Full-stack development and gaming</p>

            <h4>A little about me</h4>
            <p class="detail">
              I’ll patiently sit through a 40-hour story-driven game with zero skips,
              but waiting 30 seconds for a build pipeline to finish tests my entire sanity.
            </p>

            <h4>AI in software engineering today</h4>
            <p class="detail">
              AI is unmatched for boilerplate and syntax lookups, but can hallucinate
              subtle logical flaws that make debugging twice as tedious. It speeds up
              typing without truly understanding architecture or context; right now,
              it’s an eager junior developer whose every commit needs thorough review.
            </p>

            <h4>Where we’re headed</h4>
            <p class="detail">
              Engineering will shift from typing code to specifying requirements,
              edge cases, and architectural constraints. Autonomous agents may handle
              boilerplate, while engineers focus on verification, fault tolerance,
              and deciding what to build.
            </p>

            <div class="hot-take">
              “AI doesn’t make bad developers good; it just helps them generate
              catastrophic technical debt at record speed.”
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:Nithya.png}}" alt="Nithya">
          <div class="member-body">
            <div class="member-topline">
              <h3>Nithya</h3>
              <span class="semester">M.Sc. · 7th semester, thesis stage</span>
            </div>
            <p class="interests"><strong>Into:</strong> Distributed systems, cloud architecture, badminton, and board games</p>

            <h4>A little about me</h4>
            <p class="detail">
              I have rewritten my thesis abstract more times than I have recompiled
              my actual code.
            </p>

            <h4>AI in software engineering today</h4>
            <p class="detail">
              AI assistants are productivity multipliers for well-understood domains
              and boilerplate, but struggle with complex legacy code. They can be
              confidently wrong about synchronization and concurrency, so a fast
              copilot still needs senior oversight.
            </p>

            <h4>Where we’re headed</h4>
            <p class="detail">
              Systems integration, prompt-driven formal verification, and distributed
              consensus will matter more than routine feature programming. Junior
              roles may evolve toward system orchestration, where understanding
              failure modes and domain invariants is essential.
            </p>

            <div class="hot-take">
              “AI autocomplete hasn’t eliminated bugs; it has just made them compile
              much faster.”
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:Rafee.png}}" alt="Rafee">
          <div class="member-body">
            <div class="member-topline">
              <h3>Rafee</h3>
              <span class="semester">M.Sc. · 1st semester</span>
            </div>
            <p class="interests"><strong>Into:</strong> Frontend UI/UX, React and Next.js, table tennis, and photography</p>

            <h4>A little about me</h4>
            <p class="detail">
              I judge coffee shops entirely by their Wi-Fi stability and latency to GitHub.
            </p>

            <h4>AI in software engineering today</h4>
            <p class="detail">
              For a fresh developer, AI is an unbelievable interactive tutor that
              demystifies obscure compiler errors in seconds. But relying on it too
              early can create an illusion of competence: understanding the output
              isn’t the same as understanding the mechanics.
            </p>

            <h4>Where we’re headed</h4>
            <p class="detail">
              Natural-language intent and wireframes could compile into accessible,
              responsive interfaces. Frontend engineers will put more energy into user
              empathy, accessibility, and performant client-side state.
            </p>

            <div class="hot-take">
              “If you can’t debug code without an LLM, you are the copilot, not the agent.”
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:Raghvendra.png}}" alt="Raghvendra">
          <div class="member-body">
            <div class="member-topline">
              <h3>Raghvendra</h3>
              <span class="semester">M.Sc. · 3rd semester</span>
            </div>
            <p class="interests"><strong>Into:</strong> Machine learning infrastructure, data engineering, hiking, and chess</p>

            <h4>A little about me</h4>
            <p class="detail">
              I will spend four hours automating a manual five-minute task, and call it an investment.
            </p>

            <h4>AI in software engineering today</h4>
            <p class="detail">
              Current LLMs are incredible for rapid prototyping and translating
              business logic into SQL or boilerplate endpoints. But they lack deep
              situational context and may use deprecated methods without warning.
              Their value is reducing initial friction, not making core architectural choices.
            </p>

            <h4>Where we’re headed</h4>
            <p class="detail">
              Multi-agent pipelines may build, test, and benchmark microservices
              against synthetic workloads. Engineers will still need to define
              objectives, enforce privacy boundaries, and resolve conflicting
              business constraints.
            </p>

            <div class="hot-take">
              “90% of current ‘AI agent’ workflows are just fragile while loops
              wrapped around regex parsers.”
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:Sayemah.png}}" alt="Sayemah">
          <div class="member-body">
            <div class="member-topline">
              <h3>Sayemah</h3>
              <span class="semester">M.Sc. · 1st semester</span>
            </div>
            <p class="interests"><strong>Into:</strong> Calligraphy, cooking, traveling, and human-computer interaction</p>

            <h4>A little about me</h4>
            <p class="detail">
              I can master a complex traditional recipe on the first try, but one
              unmatched curly brace will ruin my entire evening.
            </p>

            <h4>AI in software engineering today</h4>
            <p class="detail">
              AI brings creativity and swift prototyping to engineering, lowering
              the barrier to trying novel ideas. But software is also human
              communication and interface empathy: functional code can still lack
              aesthetic intention and elegance.
            </p>

            <h4>Where we’re headed</h4>
            <p class="detail">
              Software design will become more human-centric and multidisciplinary.
              Engineers will guide agents with high-level design systems and ethical
              standards, leaving more creative energy for user delight and seamless
              interactions.
            </p>

            <div class="hot-take">
              “Prompt engineering is not the future of software engineering;
              thoughtful human design is.”
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="future-of-se" aria-labelledby="future-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Our shared point of view</p>
          <h2 id="future-title">The Future of Software Engineering</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="future-panel">
        <p class="future-lede">
          We see AI changing the mechanics of making software—not removing the need
          for engineering judgment. As agents take on more boilerplate and routine
          implementation, the human work becomes even more important: choosing the
          right problem, checking the result, and making systems work for people.
        </p>

        <div class="principles">
          <article class="principle">
            <span class="principle-number">01 / DEFINE</span>
            <h3>Make intent precise</h3>
            <p>
              Clear requirements, edge cases, and domain constraints will guide
              increasingly capable coding tools.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="principle">
            <span class="principle-number">02 / VERIFY</span>
            <h3>Earn trust with evidence</h3>
            <p>
              Testing, formal methods, code review, and failure analysis remain
              essential when generated code can look convincing.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="principle">
            <span class="principle-number">03 / CARE</span>
            <h3>Keep people in the system</h3>
            <p>
              Accessibility, privacy, thoughtful interfaces, and human oversight
              should shape how we build—not just what we build.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <h3 class="forecast-heading">Five lenses on what comes next</h3>
        <div class="forecast-list">
          <article class="forecast">
            <h4>Mohammad · Architecture and verification</h4>
            <p>
              Autonomous agents may absorb raw boilerplate work, shifting engineers
              toward requirements, architectural constraints, fault tolerance, and
              knowing what to build.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="forecast">
            <h4>Nithya · Integration and invariants</h4>
            <p>
              System orchestration, integration, and formal verification will bring
              distributed consensus and domain failure modes to the fore.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="forecast">
            <h4>Rafee · Interfaces from intent</h4>
            <p>
              Intent-driven wireframes could produce working interfaces, making
              accessibility, empathy, and high-performance client-side state a
              larger part of frontend craft.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="forecast">
            <h4>Raghvendra · Multi-agent systems</h4>
            <p>
              Agents may build and benchmark microservices, while engineers set
              objectives, protect privacy, and reconcile business constraints.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="forecast">
            <h4>Sayemah · Human-centered design</h4>
            <p>
              Engineers will steer agents with design systems and ethical standards,
              creating more room for multidisciplinary thinking and delightful
              experiences.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="footer-inner">
      <p>Built by an agent, supervised by humans. 2026 · Context Engine</p>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script>
    (() => {
      const button = document.getElementById("theme-toggle");
      const icon = button.querySelector("span");
      const root = document.documentElement;

      function updateButton(theme) {
        const isDark = theme === "dark";
        icon.textContent = isDark ? "☀" : "☾";
        button.setAttribute("aria-label", isDark ? "Switch to day mode" : "Switch to night mode");
        button.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(isDark));
      }

      updateButton(root.dataset.theme || "light");

      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const nextTheme = root.dataset.theme === "dark" ? "light" : "dark";
        root.dataset.theme = nextTheme;
        updateButton(nextTheme);
        try {
          localStorage.setItem("upb-theme", nextTheme);
        } catch (_) {
          // The theme still works for this visit if storage is unavailable.
        }
      });
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

