<h4>Fun fact</h4><p class="detail">I judge coffee shops entirely by their Wi-Fi stability and latency to GitHub.</p>
<h4>AI in software engineering today</h4><p class="detail">From a fresh developer perspective, AI is an unbelievable interactive tutor that demystifies obscure compiler errors in seconds. But relying on it too early is a trap: it creates an illusion of competence where you understand the output without understanding the underlying mechanics.</p>
<h4>Where software engineering will be in 5–10 years</h4><p class="detail">Natural language and intent-driven wireframes will directly compile into accessible, responsive user interfaces. The frontend engineer's job will focus almost entirely on user empathy, accessibility, and high-performance client-side state rather than CSS layout fighting.</p>
