<a class="skip" href="#team">Skip to team</a>
<header><div class="wrap head">
<div><a class="brand" href="#top">Context Engine</a><p class="tagline">Thoughtful engineering, human by design.</p></div>
<div class="actions"><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#team">The team</a><a href="#future-of-se">The future</a></nav><button id="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch to night mode" aria-pressed="false"><span aria-hidden="true">☾</span></button></div>
</div></header>
<main class="wrap" id="top">
<section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Agentic Software Engineering · Paderborn University</p><h1>Good engineering starts with good questions.</h1><p class="hero-copy">We’re a team of computer scientists exploring how to build software that works well, makes sense, and keeps people in the picture.</p><span class="pill">Five perspectives, one team</span></section>
<section class="section" id="team" aria-labelledby="team-title">
<p class="eyebrow">Meet the people behind the ideas</p><h2 id="team-title">The team</h2>
<p class="intro">We’re M.Sc. Computer Science students at the Agentic Software Engineering, Paderborn University lab. Curiosity about software systems and the people who depend on them connects us across interests from distributed infrastructure to human-computer interaction.</p>
<div class="grid">
<article class="card"><div class="portrait" aria-hidden="true">M</div><div class="content"><div class="name"><h3>Mohammad</h3><span class="semester">M.Sc. · 1st semester</span></div><p class="interests"><b>Interests:</b> Full-stack development, gaming</p><h4>Fun fact</h4><p class="detail">I’ll patiently sit through a 40-hour story-driven game with zero skips, but waiting 30 seconds for a build pipeline to finish tests my entire sanity.</p><h4>AI in software engineering today</h4><p class="detail">AI is unmatched for boilerplate and syntax lookups, but frequently hallucinates subtle logical flaws that make debugging twice as tedious. It speeds up typing without understanding architecture or context; every commit needs thorough code review.</p><h4>Where software engineering will be in 5–10 years</h4><p class="detail">Engineers will specify requirements, edge cases, and architectural constraints while autonomous agents handle boilerplate. Verification, fault tolerance, and knowing what to build will be central.</p><p class="take">“AI doesn’t make bad developers good; it just helps them generate catastrophic technical debt at record speed.”</p></div></article>
<article class="card"><div class="portrait" aria-hidden="true">N</div><div class="content"><div class="name"><h3>Nithya</h3><span class="semester">M.Sc. · 7th semester, thesis stage</span></div><p class="interests"><b>Interests:</b> Distributed systems, cloud architecture, badminton, board games</p><h4>Fun fact</h4><p class="detail">I have rewritten my thesis abstract more times than I have recompiled my actual code.</p><h4>AI in software engineering today</h4><p class="detail">AI multiplies productivity for well-understood domains and boilerplate, but struggles with complex legacy systems and can be confidently wrong about synchronization and concurrency. Human oversight is essential.</p><h4>Where software engineering will be in 5–10 years</h4><p class="detail">Systems integration, prompt-driven formal verification, and distributed consensus will matter more than routine feature programming. Engineers will need to know failure modes and domain invariants.</p><p class="take">“AI autocomplete hasn't eliminated bugs; it has just made them compile much faster.”</p></div></article>
<article class="card"><div class="portrait" aria-hidden="true">R</div><div class="content"><div class="name"><h3>Rafee</h3><span class="semester">M.Sc. · 1st semester</span></div><p class="interests"><b>Interests:</b> Frontend UI/UX, React/Next.js, table tennis, photography</p><h4>Fun fact</h4><p class="detail">I judge coffee shops entirely by their Wi-Fi stability and latency to GitHub.</p><h4>AI in software engineering today</h4><p class="detail">AI is an interactive tutor that demystifies obscure compiler errors. Relying on it too early risks understanding the output without understanding the mechanics.</p><h4>Where software engineering will be in 5–10 years</h4><p class="detail">Intent-driven wireframes may compile into accessible, responsive interfaces. Frontend engineers will focus on empathy, accessibility, and high-performance client-side state.</p><p class="take">“If you can't debug code without an LLM, you are the copilot, not the agent.”</p></div></article>
<article class="card"><div class="portrait" aria-hidden="true">R</div><div class="content"><div class="name"><h3>Raghvendra</h3><span class="semester">M.Sc. · 3rd semester</span></div><p class="interests"><b>Interests:</b> Machine learning infrastructure, data engineering, hiking, chess</p><h4>Fun fact</h4><p class="detail">I will spend 4 hours automating a manual 5-minute task, and call it an investment.</p><h4>AI in software engineering today</h4><p class="detail">LLMs are useful for prototyping and SQL, but lack situational context and may use deprecated methods. Their value is reducing friction, not making core architectural choices.</p><h4>Where software engineering will be in 5–10 years</h4><p class="detail">Multi-agent pipelines may build, test, and benchmark microservices. Humans will define objectives, enforce privacy boundaries, and resolve conflicting business constraints.</p><p class="take">“90% of current ‘AI agent’ workflows are just fragile while loops wrapped around regex parsers.”</p></div></article>
<article class="card"><div class="portrait" aria-hidden="true">S</div><div class="content"><div class="name"><h3>Sayemah</h3><span class="semester">M.Sc. · 1st semester</span></div><p class="interests"><b>Interests:</b> Calligraphy, culinary arts and cooking, traveling, human-computer interaction</p><h4>Fun fact</h4><p class="detail">I can master a complex traditional recipe on the first try, but one unmatched curly brace will ruin my entire evening.</p><h4>AI in software engineering today</h4><p class="detail">AI brings creativity and swift prototyping, but software also needs human communication and interface empathy. Functional code can lack aesthetic intention and elegance.</p><h4>Where software engineering will be in 5–10 years</h4><p class="detail">Software design will become more human-centric and multidisciplinary. Engineers will guide agents with design systems and ethical standards, making room for user delight and seamless interactions.</p><p class="take">“Prompt engineering is not the future of software engineering; thoughtful human design is.”</p></div></article>
</div></section>
<section class="section" id="future-of-se" aria-labelledby="future-title"><p class="eyebrow">Our shared perspective</p><h2 id="future-title">The Future of Software Engineering</h2>
<div class="future"><p class="future-copy">AI will change how software is made, not remove the need for engineering judgment. As agents take on routine implementation, engineers will define problems, verify results, and ensure systems serve people.</p>
<div class="future-grid"><article><b>Define intent</b><p>Requirements, edge cases, and domain constraints guide capable tools.</p></article><article><b>Verify with evidence</b><p>Testing, formal methods, code review, and failure analysis remain essential.</p></article><article><b>Keep people central</b><p>Accessibility, privacy, thoughtful interfaces, and human oversight shape good software.</p></article><article><b>Build resilient systems</b><p>Integration, distributed systems, orchestration, and fault tolerance will matter.</p></article></div></div>
</section>
</main>
<footer><div class="wrap"><p>Built by an agent, supervised by humans. 2026 · Context Engine</p></div></footer>
<script>
(()=>{const r=document.documentElement,b=document.getElementById("theme-toggle"),i=b.querySelector("span");function update(){const d=r.dataset.theme==="dark";i.textContent=d?"☀":"☾";b.setAttribute("aria-label",d?"Switch to day mode":"Switch to night mode");b.setAttribute("aria-pressed",String(d))}update();b.addEventListener("click",()=>{r.dataset.theme=r.dataset.theme==="dark"?"light":"dark";try{localStorage.setItem("upb-theme",r.dataset.theme)}catch(e){}update()})})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
